From: Alessio Ferri <alessio.ferri@mythread.it>
Date: Thu, 6 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] b43: program the fifth transmit power-up override on N-PHY
 rev 7

b43_nphy_rf_ctl_override_one_to_many() makes four calls for
N_RF_CTL_OVER_CMD_TX_PU. brcmsmac's wlc_phy_rfctrl_override_1tomany_nphy()
makes five: field (0x1 << 2) on override 2 sits between (0x1 << 0) on
override 2 and (0x1 << 11) on override 1, and b43 does not have it.

An MMIO capture of wl 6.30.102.7 on a BCM6362 (N-PHY rev 8, radio 2057
rev 8) shows the operations: the setup of the PAPD calibration switches
the transmit power up on the core being calibrated and off on the other
one, and each of those two calls produces a pair on 0x0346/0x0344 and
0x0347/0x0345 with mask 0x0004 that the port does not emit.

The other four commands of the one to many path have as many calls as
brcmsmac, so this is the only one missing.

Verified: records #11776-#11777 and #11786-#11787, from
"PHY.OR   addr=0x0346 val=0x0004 (set 0x0004)"
Link: https://git.kernel.org/pub/scm/linux/kernel/git/torvalds/linux.git/tree/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmsmac/phy/phy_n.c?id=848acc8ffe1b#n21406
Link: https://github.com/aleferri/b43-6362-wip/blob/04e05f5/router-data/dsl-3580l/opinit-ch1-ch6-bw20.decoded
Link: https://github.com/aleferri/b43-6362-wip/blob/04e05f5/test/phase_compare.py, region papd-cal

Signed-off-by: Alessio Ferri <alessio.ferri@mythread.it>
---
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/phy_n.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/phy_n.c
@@ -220,6 +220,7 @@ static void b43_nphy_rf_ctl_override_one_to_many(struct b43_wldev *dev,
 		b43_nphy_rf_ctl_override_rev7(dev, 0x4, value, core, off, 0);
 		b43_nphy_rf_ctl_override_rev7(dev, 0x2, value, core, off, 1);
 		b43_nphy_rf_ctl_override_rev7(dev, 0x1, value, core, off, 2);
+		b43_nphy_rf_ctl_override_rev7(dev, 0x4, value, core, off, 2);
 		b43_nphy_rf_ctl_override_rev7(dev, 0x0800, 1, core, off, 1);
 		break;
 	case N_RF_CTL_OVER_CMD_RX_GAIN:
